{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Counts</b> — Because he mentioned the outcasts of Israel, who are scattered throughout the earth, he set against this: \"counts a number to the stars,\" for the stars are scattered in the upper sphere, and He knows them all. Now there is a difference between מונה and מספר, for מספר is the particular and מונה is the counting of the whole, close to the derivation of מנין." "<b>To all of them names He calls</b> — And the meaning is like: not one is missing. And this is true and correct."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 147, :notes {0 "I read the last phrase as explaining that מונה derives from the root מנין (counting), making it denote the act of numbering the totality."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:59.424070231Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}